   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "366582f7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Quick CLI Sanity Check\n",
    "\n",
    "Run inference via the `yolo` CLI directly on the trained weights, just to\n",
    "confirm the model loads and produces predictions before writing the full\n",
    "Python inference/visualization code below."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f8c6552b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!yolo predict model={BEST_WEIGHTS} source={TEST_IMAGES[0]} conf=0.25"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1e3ab3f2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Inference & Visualization\n",
    "\n",
    "Load the trained model in Python and draw the predicted lane/T-mark masks\n",
    "directly on the image, with a label + confidence score placed at each mask's\n",
    "centroid. `t_mark` labels are nudged above the mask so they don't overlap the\n",
    "line labels.\n",
    "\n",
    "Written as a reusable function so it can be run against multiple test images below."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7246b756",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from ultralytics import YOLO\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "model = YOLO(BEST_WEIGHTS)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def predict_and_plot(image_path, model=model):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Run segmentation inference on one image and plot masks with\n",
    "    class + confidence labels centered on each detected region.\"\"\"\n",
    "    results = model(image_path)\n",
    "    result = results[0]\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Draw masks only (boxes/labels/conf handled manually below for more control)\n",
    "    img = result.plot(boxes=False, labels=False, conf=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "    plt.figure(figsize=(6, 10))\n",
    "    plt.imshow(img)\n",
    "\n",
    "    if result.masks is not None:\n",
    "        for i, mask in enumerate(result.masks.xy):\n",
    "            cls = int(result.boxes[i].cls.cpu())\n",
    "            conf = float(result.boxes[i].conf.cpu())\n",
    "            name = result.names[cls]\n",
    "\n",
    "            cx = np.mean(mask[:, 0])\n",
    "            cy = np.mean(mask[:, 1])\n",
    "\n",
    "            if name == \"lane\":\n",
    "                x, y, fontsize = cx, cy, 10\n",
    "            else:  # t_mark\n",
    "                x, y, fontsize = cx, max(10, cy - 20), 6\n",
    "\n",
    "            plt.text(\n",
    "                x, y, f\"{name} {conf:.2f}\",\n",
    "                color=\"white\", fontsize=fontsize,\n",
    "                ha=\"center\", va=\"center\",\n",
    "                bbox=dict(facecolor=\"black\", alpha=0.7, boxstyle=\"round,pad=0.3\"),\n",
    "            )\n",
    "\n",
    "    plt.axis(\"off\")\n",
    "    plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "    plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "28c1df91",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Results\n",
    "\n",
    "Running the model on a few different test images to check how well it\n",
    "generalizes across viewpoints (above-water POV vs. a pool with many lane\n",
    "lines visible)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "c6b93639",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "predict_and_plot(TEST_IMAGES[0])  # single-lane POV shot"
   ]
  },
